Tugboat is a monorepo with per-module licensing. There is no single license
covering the whole repository.

  - engine, bridge, xo ........ Mozilla Public License 2.0
  - all other modules ......... MIT License

Each module directory contains its own LICENSE file, which is authoritative for
everything in that directory, including its build script. Files in the MPL
modules also carry an SPDX-License-Identifier line.

Three shared build files at the repository root are MIT: settings.gradle.kts,
build.gradle.kts, and gradle/libs.versions.toml. They belong to no single
module and configure the MPL and MIT modules alike; each carries an SPDX header
saying so.

See LICENSING.md at the repository root for what this means in practice.

